pcbkit 2

// AO3401A (Alpha & Omega Semiconductor): P-channel MOSFET, -30 V, -4 A, 60 mohm at -4.5 V gate,
// logic level (-2.5 V rated), SOT-23: a high-side load switch or reverse-polarity protection
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/AO3401A.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet: https://www.aosmd.com/res/datasheets/AO3401A.pdf (Rev 3.1, December 2023)
// Pins: AO3401A datasheet Rev 3.1, SOT23 top view (p. 1): gate and source on the side with the pin
// 1 mark, drain alone (JEDEC SOT-23 numbering 1 G, 2 S, 3 D; the drawing draws no numbers),
// absolute maximum ratings and electrical characteristics
// Footprint: the standard package `SOT-23`
// Symbol: digikey-kicad d4bd68f42e6ccc474526811a853a03692e170b58
// dk_Transistors-FETs-MOSFETs-Single:AO3401A (CC-BY-SA-4.0),
// https://github.com/Digi-Key/digikey-kicad-library
// 3D model: kicad 10.0.7 Package_TO_SOT_SMD.3dshapes/SOT-23 (the model of
// Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23: the package `SOT-23`) (CC-BY-SA-4.0)
// Parameters: digikey-kicad d4bd68f42e6ccc474526811a853a03692e170b58
// dk_Transistors-FETs-MOSFETs-Single:AO3401A (CC-BY-SA-4.0),
// https://github.com/Digi-Key/digikey-kicad-library
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: High-side switch: source to the supply, drain to the load; pull the gate to the source
// (100 kohm) so it stays off, and pull it low (an NPN or N-MOSFET such as 2N7002, or a GPIO when
// the supply is the GPIO's own) to turn it on. A 3.3 V GPIO can switch a 3.3 V rail directly; a 5
// V rail needs the level shift.
// Note: Reverse-polarity protection: drain to the input connector, source to the circuit, gate to
// GND (with a zener from gate to source above 12 V supplies): the body diode conducts first, then
// the channel shorts it.
// Note: 125 °C/W steady state: keep it under about 1 W at 25 °C ambient, with copper on the
// drain.

/// AO3401A — P-channel MOSFET, -30 V, -4 A, 60 mohm at -4.5 V gate, logic level (-2.5 V rated),
/// SOT-23: a high-side load switch or reverse-polarity protection
part Part = device(
  footprint = (sot23(3)) with { models = [Model3d { path = "Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23" }] },
  prefix = "Q",
  mpn = "AO3401A",
  manufacturer = "Alpha & Omega Semiconductor",
  pinout = { G = "1", S = "2", D = "3" },
  pinTypes = { G = io.input(max = 12V), S = .passive, D = .passive },
) with {
  fields {
    Status = "checked"
    PinoutSource = "AO3401A datasheet Rev 3.1, SOT23 top view (p. 1): gate and source on the side with the pin 1 mark, drain alone (JEDEC SOT-23 numbering 1 G, 2 S, 3 D; the drawing draws no numbers), absolute maximum ratings and electrical characteristics"
    Datasheet = "https://www.aosmd.com/res/datasheets/AO3401A.pdf"
  }
}
